{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-drawn icons for the memory game, shared by every lesson.",
    "A vocabulary entry in a lesson.json may carry \"icon\": \"<name>\", and",
    "build.py inlines the markup below when it writes 15-memory.html. The",
    "markup is the inside of an <svg> only; build.py wraps it with the viewBox",
    "and the stroke attributes here, so every icon is one colour, scales to any",
    "size, needs no file of its own and no icon font, and works with no",
    "connection. Single colour on purpose: it inherits currentColor, so dark",
    "mode needs no second drawing.",
    "Names describe the picture, not the word, so a later lesson can point a",
    "different word at the same drawing. Only concrete words get one; abstract",
    "words pair with their English meaning instead."
  ],
